b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-3\"><sup><i><b>d</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-4\"><sup><i><b>e</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-5\"><sup><i><b>f</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-6\"><sup><i><b>g</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-7\"><sup><i><b>h</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-8\"><sup><i><b>i</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-9\"><sup><i><b>j</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Haberman_&amp;_Swan_2023_67-10\"><sup><i><b>k</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFHabermanSwan2023\" class=\"citation news cs1\"><a href=\"/wiki/Maggie_Haberman\" title=\"Maggie Haberman\">Haberman, Maggie</a>; <a href=\"/wiki/Jonathan_Swan\" title=\"Jonathan Swan\">Swan, Jonathan</a> (April 20, 2023). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/20/us/politics/republican-president-2024-heritage-foundation.html\">\"Heritage Foundation Makes Plans to Staff Next G.O.P. Administration\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_New_York_Times\" title=\"The New York Times\">The New York Times</a></i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230913101937/https://www.nytimes.com/2023/04/20/us/politics/republican-president-2024-heritage-foundation.html\">Archived</a> from the original on September 13, 2023<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">July 7,</span> 2024</span>. <q>But for this election, after conservatives and Mr. Trump himself decried what they viewed as terrible staffing decisions made during his administration, more than 50 conservative groups have temporarily set aside rivalries to team up with Heritage on the project, set to start Friday.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Heritage+Foundation+Makes+Plans+to+Staff+Next+G.O.P.+Administration&amp;rft.date=2023-04-20&amp;rft.aulast=Haberman&amp;rft.aufirst=Maggie&amp;rft.au=Swan%2C+Jonathan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2023%2F04%2F20%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Frepublican-president-2024-heritage-foundation.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-68\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-68\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite class=\"citation news cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.councilofnonprofits.org/running-nonprofit/governance-leadership/political-campaign-activities-risks-tax-exempt-status\">\"Political Campaign Activities – Risks to Tax-Exempt Status\"</a>. National Council of Nonprofits. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240613152915/https://www.councilofnonprofits.org/running-nonprofit/governance-leadership/political-campaign-activities-risks-tax-exempt-status\">Archived</a> from the original on June 13, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">June 12,</span> 2024</span>. <q>In return for its favored tax-status, a 501(c)(3) charitable nonprofit, foundation, or religious organization promises the federal government that it will not engage in \"political campaign activity\".</q></cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Political+Campaign+Activities+%E2%80%93+Risks+to+Tax-Exempt+Status&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.councilofnonprofits.org%2Frunning-nonprofit%2Fgovernance-leadership%2Fpolitical-campaign-activities-risks-tax-exempt-status&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-69\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-69\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFSerwer2024\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Serwer, Adam (August 1, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/08/trump-project-2025-director-weird/679321/\">\"Why Trump Can't Banish the Weirdos\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Atlantic\" title=\"The Atlantic\">The Atlantic</a></i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20241009121239/https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/08/trump-project-2025-director-weird/679321/\">Archived</a> from the original on October 9, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">August 5,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Atlantic&amp;rft.atitle=Why+Trump+Can%27t+Banish+the+Weirdos&amp;rft.date=2024-08-01&amp;rft.aulast=Serwer&amp;rft.aufirst=Adam&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theatlantic.com%2Fpolitics%2Farchive%2F2024%2F08%2Ftrump-project-2025-director-weird%2F679321%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-70\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-70\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMacGillis2024\" class=\"citation web cs1\">MacGillis, Alec (August 1, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.propublica.org/article/project-2025-trump-campaign-heritage-foundation-paul-dans\">\"The Man Behind Project 2025's Most Radical Plans\"</a>. <i>ProPublica</i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20241009121203/https://www.propublica.org/article/project-2025-trump-campaign-heritage-foundation-paul-dans\">Archived</a> from the original on October 9, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">August 14,</span> 2024</span>. <q>The most important pillar of Project 2025 has always been about personnel, not policy. Or rather, the whole effort is animated by the Reagan-era maxim that personnel is policy, that power flows from having the right people in the right jobs.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=ProPublica&amp;rft.atitle=The+Man+Behind+Project+2025%27s+Most+Radical+Plans&amp;rft.date=2024-08-01&amp;rft.aulast=MacGillis&amp;rft.aufirst=Alec&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.propublica.org%2Farticle%2Fproject-2025-trump-campaign-heritage-foundation-paul-dans&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-71\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-71\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFHartmann2024\" class=\"citation magazine cs1\">Hartmann, Margaret (June 28, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/trumps-second-term-agenda.html\">\"Trump's Most Unhinged Plans for His Second Term\"</a>. Early and Often (story series). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Intelligencer_(website)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Intelligencer (website)\">Intelligencer</a></i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240330201440/https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/trumps-second-term-agenda.html\">Archived</a> from the original on March 30, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 6,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Intelligencer&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Most+Unhinged+Plans+for+His+Second+Term&amp;rft.date=2024-06-28&amp;rft.aulast=Hartmann&amp;rft.aufirst=Margaret&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnymag.com%2Fintelligencer%2Farticle%2Ftrumps-second-term-agenda.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-The_Heritage_Foundation_2023-73\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-The_Heritage_Foundation_2023_73-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-The_Heritage_Foundation_2023_73-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1 cs1-prop-unfit\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20231120155902/https://www.heritage.org/press/project-2025-publishes-comprehensive-policy-guide-mandate-leadership-the-conservative-promise\">\"Project 2025 Publishes Comprehensive Policy Guide, 'Mandate for Leadership: The Conservative Promise'<span class=\"cs1-kern-right\"></span>\"</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/The_Heritage_Foundation\" title=\"The Heritage Foundation\">The Heritage Foundation</a>. April 21, 2023. Archived from the original on November 20, 2023<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 19,</span> 2023</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Project+2025+Publishes+Comprehensive+Policy+Guide%2C+%27Mandate+for+Leadership%3A+The+Conservative+Promise%27&amp;rft.pub=The+Heritage+Foundation&amp;rft.date=2023-04-21&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.heritage.org%2Fpress%2Fproject-2025-publishes-comprehensive-policy-guide-mandate-leadership-the-conservative-promise&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Leingang-2024-74\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Leingang-2024_74-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Leingang-2024_74-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Leingang-2024_74-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Leingang-2024_74-3\"><sup><i><b>d</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Leingang-2024_74-4\"><sup><i><b>e</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFLeingang2024\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Leingang, Rachel (July 9, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump\">\"What is Project 2025 and what is Trump's involvement?\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Guardian\" title=\"The Guardian\">The Guardian</a></i>. <a href=\"/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ISSN (identifier)\">ISSN</a>&#160;<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/issn/0261-3077\">0261-3077</a>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240613152914/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/26/what-is-project-2025-trump\">Archived</a> from the original on June 13, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">July 9,</span> 2024</span>. <q>Still, Heritage claimed credit for a bevy of Trump policy proposals in his first term, based on the group's 2017 version of the Mandate for Leadership. The group calculated that 64% of its policy recommendations were implemented or proposed by Trump in some way during his first year in office.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=What+is+Project+2025+and+what+is+Trump%27s+involvement%3F&amp;rft.date=2024-07-09&amp;rft.issn=0261-3077&amp;rft.aulast=Leingang&amp;rft.aufirst=Rachel&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2Farticle%2F2024%2Fmay%2F26%2Fwhat-is-project-2025-trump&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-quinn_blueprint-75\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-quinn_blueprint_75-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-quinn_blueprint_75-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFQuinnRosen2024\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Quinn, Melissa; Rosen, Jacob (July 8, 2024). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/what-is-project-2025-trump-conservative-blueprint-heritage-foundation/\">\"What is Project 2025? What to know about the conservative blueprint for a second Trump administration\"</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/CBS_News\" title=\"CBS News\">CBS News</a>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240710042242/https://www.cbsnews.com/news/what-is-project-2025-trump-conservative-blueprint-heritage-foundation/\">Archived</a> from the original on July 10, 2024<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">July 10,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=What+is+Project+2025%3F+What+to+know+about+the+conservative+blueprint+for+a+second+Trump+administration&amp;rft.date=2024-07-08&amp;rft.aulast=Quinn&amp;rft.aufirst=Melissa&amp;rft.au=Rosen%2C+Jacob&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cbsnews.com%2Fnews%2Fwhat-is-project-2025-trump-conservative-blueprint-heritage-foundation%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Doyle_2023-76\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">^ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Doyle_2023_76-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Doyle_2023_76-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1238218222\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFDoyle2023\" class=\"citation news cs1\">Doyle, Katherine (November 17, 2023). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/donations-surged-groups-linked-conservative-project-2025-rcna125638\">\"Donations Have Surged to Groups Linked to Conservative Project 2025\"</a>. <i><a href=\"/wiki/NBC_News\" title=\"NBC News\">NBC News</a></i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20231118071504/https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/donations-surged-groups-linked-conservative-project-2025-rcna125638\">Archived</a> from the original on November 18, 2023<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">November 18,</span> 2023</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=NBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=Donations+Have+Surged+to+Groups+Linked+to+Conservative+Project+2025&amp;rft.date=2023-11-17&amp;rft.aulast=Doyle&amp;rft.aufirst=Katherine&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nbcnews.com%2Fpolitics%2F2024-election%2Fdonations-surged-groups-linked-conservative-project-2025-rcna125638&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AProject+2025\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-harris1-77\"><span class=\"mw-cite-b